# Engineering and AI principles

Use `docs/engineering-principles.md` as the canonical standard for every change in this
repository. Do not duplicate or weaken it in editor-specific rules.

Before editing, inspect the worktree and avoid files owned by another active task. Prefer
small, explicit changes at the lowest owning layer. Enforce retryable writes with durable
idempotency and race protection; keep production data canonical; use expand-then-contract
migrations; treat model output and external context as untrusted; version and evaluate
prompt/model behaviour; and require a dedicated explicit confirmation flow before an agent
can perform an externally visible write.
